    {
      "id": 24635,
      "name": "Christopher",
      "username": "Christopher",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
      "created_at": "2011-12-17T19:05:56.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Yes, Decoy Projection is <span class=\"bbcode-b\">absolutely</span> a Hero Target.  Think about it this way: The Enraged T-Rex is an Environment card, as it comes from an Environment deck.  It is also a Target, as it has HP.  Therefore, it is an Environment Target.<br>\nBlade Battalion is a Villain Card as it comes from a Villain Deck.  It is also a Target, as it has HP.  Therefore, it is a Villain Target.<br>\nThus, Decoy Projection, a Hero Card from a Hero Deck that also has HP, is certainly a Hero Target.</p>\n<p>So, when the Gene-Bound Frosthound deals 2 cold damage to each Hero Target, the Decoy Projection takes 2 damage from the Frosthound AND 2 damage redirected from The Visionary.  Of course, if it only had 1 or 2 HP when this happened, it would be wise to have it take damage from The Visionary before it took its own damage.  But that’s more strategy and less definition.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:58:36.731Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
