      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Yes, Decoy Projection is [b]absolutely[/b] a Hero Target.  Think about it this way: The Enraged T-Rex is an Environment card, as it comes from an Environment deck.  It is also a Target, as it has HP.  Therefore, it is an Environment Target.  \nBlade Battalion is a Villain Card as it comes from a Villain Deck.  It is also a Target, as it has HP.  Therefore, it is a Villain Target.\nThus, Decoy Projection, a Hero Card from a Hero Deck that also has HP, is certainly a Hero Target.\n\nSo, when the Gene-Bound Frosthound deals 2 cold damage to each Hero Target, the Decoy Projection takes 2 damage from the Frosthound AND 2 damage redirected from The Visionary.  Of course, if it only had 1 or 2 HP when this happened, it would be wise to have it take damage from The Visionary before it took its own damage.  But that's more strategy and less definition.",
